-personalization \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel\n\n# Interactive session (no self-modification, load agents via C-c a inside Emacs)\n./utils/iar.sh \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel\n#+end_src\n\n*** Autonomous Loops (=--loop=)\n\nRuns an agent for N cycles with cooldown between each. Sends Telegram notifications if =AGENT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN= and =AGENT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID= are set. Container names are auto-suffixed with PID so multiple loops can run in parallel without collisions.\n\n#+begin_src bash\n# Darwin autonomous loop (code changes, self-modification enabled)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --self-modification \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent darwin \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel \\\n  --max-cycles 50\n\n# Gardener autonomous loop (prompt refinement, no self-modification)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent gardener \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel \\\n  --max-cycles 10\n\n# Playground loop on GPU model (sophon, 120B, 128K context)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent playground \\\n  --model nemotron-3-super:120b \\\n  --ctx 131072 \\\n  --ollama-host 10.66.0.5:11434 \\\n  --max-cycles 999 \\\n  --cooldown 300\n\n# Playground loop on CPU model (daftpunk, 30B, 128K context)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent playground \\\n  --model granite4.1:30b \\\n  --ctx 131072 \\\n  --ollama-host 10.66.0.3:11434 \\\n  --max-cycles 999 \\\n  --cooldown 300\n#+end_src\n\n*** Model and Host Selection\n\nThe =--model= and =--ctx= flags control which LLM runs and how much context window it gets. These are critical for local models -- the KV cache scales linearly with context size, so a 120B model at 1M context would need ~320GB of RAM just for the cache.\n\n| Flag | Default | Description |\n|------+---------+-------------|\n| =--model N